{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\user\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -LiteralPath \\\"C:\\\\Projects\\\\Agent_Workspace\\\\HG-KSEOS\\\\var\\\\swof-construction-002-w2-repair-001\\\\specs\\\\R1_WO-SWOF-W2-R001_SPEC.md\\\" -Raw\"","aggregated_output":"# R1 WO-SWOF-W2-R001 — Security rights/HumanGate currentness and exact-bound approval repair\n\nrepair_id: SWOF-W2-CLOSURE-R1\norder_id: SWOF-CONSTRUCTION-002-W2-REPAIR-001\nrepair_class: W2_EXTERNAL_CHALLENGE_SMALLEST_REPAIR\nsource_candidate_sha: bffe540ffbab683127338a4bd94b2f7d4bb39cce\ncanonical_law: PI-PKG-06::DOC-03 (ApprovalTokenSchema, TOK-INV-001..014, §16.1A token time validity)\nconfirmed_defects: F-W2-EXT-001 (rights currentness fail-open), F-W2-EXT-002 (HumanGate syntactic-only)\n\n## 0. Why this repair exists (raw repro, not report prose)\n\nProbes on the exact source bytes produced:\n\n```\nR-C1.1  check_rights(expired_scope, 'doc.read')            -> {\"allowed\": true, \"reason\": \"ENTITLED\"}   FAIL-OPEN\nR-C1.8  assert_credential_scope(expired_scope,'api.call')  -> returned None (no raise)                   FAIL-OPEN\nR-C2.1  assert_human_gate_satisfied(route,'sure go ahead') -> returned None (no raise)                   FAIL-OPEN\nR-C2.3  assert_human_gate_satisfied(route,'sure go ahead', requesting_actor='bob') -> no raise           FAIL-OPEN\n```\n\nRoot causes: `_expired()` returns False when `now is None`; `assert_credential_scope()` never consults\n`expires_at`; `assert_human_gate_satisfied()` accepts any non-empty string that is not the requesting\nactor and has no token structure at all.\n\n## 1. Files you may write (exactly these, nothing else)\n\n```\nsrc/security/rights.py            (modify)\nsrc/security/humangate.py         (create)\nsrc/security/__init__.py          (modify: export the new names)\nsrc/security/tests/test_rights.py               (modify: update the cases that encoded the narrower law)\nsrc/security/tests/test_humangate_currentness.py (create)\nschemas/security/approval_token.schema.json       (create)\nschemas/security/rights_currentness.schema.json   (create)\n```\n\nPython standard library only. ASCII only. LF line endings. Do not touch any other path, do not touch\nHG-KSEOS or any other project.\n\n## 2. rights.py — currentness must be a required decision input\n\n### 2.1 `_expired(scope, now)` must fail closed\n\n```\nexpires is None                       -> False  (no expiry: nothing to evaluate)\nexpires malformed / not ISO-8601 UTC  -> True   (unknown expiry = expired)\nnow is None                           -> True   (CHANGED: unknown currentness = expired)\nnow malformed                         -> True\notherwise                             -> now >= expires   (equality at expiry IS expired)\n```\n\n### 2.2 `check_rights(scope, entitlement, *, now=None, subject=None)`\n\nKeep the existing order of checks (scope validity, subject mismatch, entitlement validity, revoked) but\nreplace the expiry handling with a distinct, ordered pair so the reason code is exact:\n\n```\nif scope.expires_at is not None and now is None:\n    return RightsDecision(False, \"CURRENTNESS_UNAVAILABLE_FAIL_CLOSED\", False)\nif _expired(scope, now):\n    return RightsDecision(False, \"EXPIRED\", False)\n```\n\nNote: a scope with `expires_at=None` and `now=None` is still allowed to return ENTITLED (nothing to\nevaluate) — that is the positive control and must not regress.\n\n### 2.3 `assert_credential_scope(scope, use, *, subject=None, now=None)`\n\nAdd currentness and expiry. Keep the existing checks (scope validity, subject mismatch, use validity,\nrevoked, membership). Insert before the membership check:\n\n```\nif scope.expires_at is not None and now is None:\n    raise RightsDenied(\"CURRENTNESS_UNAVAILABLE_FAIL_CLOSED\")\nif _expired(scope, now):\n    raise RightsDenied(\"EXPIRED_CREDENTIAL_SCOPE\")\n```\n\nAlso export a helper `currentness_required(scope) -> bool` returning `scope.expires_at is not None`, so a\ncaller can decide to supply trusted currentness before calling.\n\n## 3. humangate.py — one typed exact-bound ApprovalToken at the existing seam\n\nDo NOT build a second authority system and do NOT invent cryptography. The token is a value object; the\nverifier is the authority. Signature verification is delegated to an injected trusted key registry and\nFAILS CLOSED when the registry or the key is unavailable.\n\n### 3.1 Canonical field set (PI-PKG-06::DOC-03 §15, ApprovalToken 1.0.0)\n\n`ApprovalToken` is a frozen dataclass carrying at least:\n`token_id, request_id, decision_id, subject, subject_hash, semantic_version, actor, operation,\ntarget_system, resource (tuple[str,...]), environment, purpose_ref, scope (tuple[str,...]), data_class,\neffect_digest, consumer_audience_hash, approver, authority_class, approver_authn_context_ref,\nauthn_assurance_class, reauthenticated_at, authn_session_generation, credential_generation,\napproval_basis_hash, independent_checker_required, independent_checker_evidence_ref,\nissued_at, expires_at, nonce, rollback_ref, token_state, consumer, integrity_profile_id, issuer_id,\nkey_id, key_generation, signature`\n\n`token_state` is one of `ACTIVE | CONSUMED | REVOKED | EXPIRED`.\n`integrity_profile_id` is the constant `\"SWOF-HG-INTEGRITY-001\"`.\nDigest fields must be 64 lowercase hex; `signature` must be 86 base64url chars; `scope` and `resource`\nmust be non-empty tuples of unique strings (compare as sets).\n\n### 3.2 `ApprovalRequest` — what is being approved\n\nFrozen dataclass: `subject, subject_hash, semantic_version, actor, operation, target_system, resource,\nenvironment, purpose_ref, scope, data_class, effect_digest, consumer_audience_hash, effect_risk_tier,\npermission_class, autonomy_tier, required_authority, rollback_ref, independent_checker_required`.\n\n### 3.3 `VerificationContext` — the current-at-commit inputs\n\nFrozen dataclass: `commit_time` (RFC3339 UTC, trusted), `rights_generation, consent_generation,\nsecurity_policy_generation, provider_generation, ruin_generation, authn_session_generation,\ncredential_generation, key_generation, revocation_generation` (all `int | None`),\n`expected_consumer_audience_hash`, `trusted_key_registry` (callable `(issuer_id, key_id, key_generation)\n-> bool` or None), `nonce_ledger` (object with `reserve(nonce) -> bool`), `independent_checker_evidence_ref`,\n`max_reauth_age_seconds`.\n\n### 3.4 `verify_approval_token(token, request, ctx) -> ApprovalDecision`\n\nFirst-fail, deterministic, in this exact order. `ApprovalDecision` is a frozen dataclass\n`(ok: bool, code: str, detail: str)`. Every failure returns `ok=False` with the SI code; never raise for\na merely-invalid token (raise only for a non-canonical input object type).\n\n```\n1  not isinstance(token, ApprovalToken)                    -> ok=False, \"NOT_A_CANONICAL_APPROVAL_TOKEN\"\n2  shape validation (§3.1)                                 -> \"DENY_TOKEN_SCHEMA\"   (incl. wrong\n                                                              integrity_profile_id, bad digests, bad sig shape)\n3  token.token_state != \"ACTIVE\"                           -> \"DENY_TOKEN_STATE\"            (TOK-INV-004)\n4  exact binding vs request: subject, subject_hash, semantic_version, actor, operation, target_system,\n   resource(set), environment, purpose_ref, scope(set), data_class, effect_digest, consumer_audience_hash\n                                                            -> \"DENY_EXACT_BINDING\"          (TOK-INV-002)\n5  audience: ctx.expected_consumer_audience_hash set AND != token.consumer_audience_hash\n                                                            -> \"DENY_AUDIENCE_MISMATCH\"      (TOK-INV-011)\n6  time: commit_time missing/malformed                     -> \"DENY_TOKEN_TIME\"\n   issued_at <= commit_time < expires_at strictly          -> \"DENY_TOKEN_TIME\"             (TOK-INV-003)\n   equality at expires_at is INVALID\n7  false authority: approver/actor must be a human principal ref\n   (prefix \"human:\"), never a model/tool/provider/agent/mcp/a2a/automation ref\n                                                            -> \"DENY_FALSE_AUTHORITY\"        (TOK-INV-008, -012)\n8  authn: authn_assurance_class in {AAC1,AAC2,AAC3};\n   reauthenticated_at present, well-formed and within ctx.max_reauth_age_seconds of commit_time\n                                                            -> \"DENY_AUTHN\"                  (TOK-INV-013)\n9  generations current-at-commit: for every generation present in ctx (non-None), the token's matching\n   generation must exist and be equal; a token missing a generation the context requires is stale\n                                                            -> \"DENY_STALE_GENERATION\"       (TOK-INV-006)\n10 rollback: request.effect_risk_tier in {\"P3\",\"P4\",\"P5\"} or permission_class in {\"P3\",\"P4\",\"P5\"}\n   requires a non-empty token.rollback_ref == request.rollback_ref\n                                                            -> \"DENY_NO_ROLLBACK\"            (TOK-INV-007)\n11 integrity: ctx.trusted_key_registry is None              -> \"DENY_TOKEN_INTEGRITY\"\n   registry(issuer_id,key_id,key_generation) is not True    -> \"DENY_TOKEN_INTEGRITY\"        (TOK-INV-010)\n12 replay/consume-once: ctx.nonce_ledger is None              -> \"DENY_REPLAY\"\n   ledger.reserve(token.nonce) is not True                   -> \"DENY_REPLAY\"                 (TOK-INV-005)\n   (reserve must succeed exactly once per nonce; a second reserve returns False)\n13 T3: request.autonomy_tier == \"T3\" requires\n   token.independent_checker_required is True AND\n   ctx.independent_checker_evidence_ref non-empty AND\n   token.independent_checker_evidence_ref == ctx.independent_checker_evidence_ref\n                                                            -> \"DENY_T3_CHECKER\"             (TOK-INV-014)\n14 otherwise                                                -> ok=True, \"APPROVE_BASIS_SATISFIED\"\n```\n\nOrdering rule: checks 1-6 are structural/identity, 7-13 are authority/currentness. Do not reorder.\nEvery code above is a literal string; keep them exact.\n\nAlso provide:\n\n- `class NonceLedger` — in-memory consume-once store, `reserve(nonce) -> bool`, thread-safe with a\n  `threading.Lock`, reject non-str/empty nonce. Second reserve of the same nonce returns False.\n- `assert_human_gate_satisfied(route, approval, *, requesting_actor=None, request=None, ctx=None)`:\n  - keep the existing behaviour for `route` (unknown route -> `HumanGateBypassAttempt(\"UNKNOWN_ROUTE_FAIL_CLOSED\")`,\n    `not route.required` -> return).\n  - for a required route, `approval` MUST be an `ApprovalToken` and `request`/`ctx` MUST be supplied;\n    anything else raises `HumanGateBypassAttempt` with the exact code:\n    - not an ApprovalToken, or request/ctx missing -> `\"NOT_A_CANONICAL_APPROVAL_TOKEN\"`\n    - verifier failure -> `HumanGateBypassAttempt(decision.code)`\n    - `approval.approver` equal to `requesting_actor` (after strip) -> `\"SELF_APPROVAL_REFUSED\"`\n    - verified -> return None\n  - a bare non-empty string MUST now raise `\"NOT_A_CANONICAL_APPROVAL_TOKEN\"`. That is the whole point of\n    this repair: a syntactic string is no longer an approval.\n\n## 4. Schemas\n\n`schemas/security/approval_token.schema.json` — JSON Schema (draft 2020-12) mirroring §3.1 required\nfields, `additionalProperties: false`, enums for `token_state` and `authn_assurance_class`, digest\npatterns `^[0-9a-f]{64}$`, signature pattern `^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{86}$`, `integrity_profile_id` const\n`SWOF-HG-INTEGRITY-001`, and the conditional `independent_checker_evidence_ref` requirement when\n`independent_checker_required` is true.\n\n`schemas/security/rights_currentness.schema.json` — JSON Schema for a `RightsScope`-shaped object with\n`expires_at` nullable RFC3339 UTC and the rule encoded in prose + `description` fields that a scope with\n`expires_at != null` cannot be evaluated without a trusted `now`.\n\n## 5. Tests you MUST add or update (this is the acceptance evidence)\n\n### 5.1 `src/security/tests/test_humangate_currentness.py` (create)\n\nRights currentness:\n```\n1  expired entitlement + now omitted            -> allowed False, reason CURRENTNESS_UNAVAILABLE_FAIL_CLOSED\n2  expired entitlement + now past expiry        -> allowed False, reason EXPIRED\n3  now == expires_at boundary                   -> allowed False, reason EXPIRED\n4  malformed now                                -> allowed False\n5  revoked scope                                -> allowed False, reason REVOKED\n6  no-expiry scope + now omitted                -> allowed True  (positive control, must not regress)\n7  no-expiry scope + now supplied               -> allowed True\n8  expired credential scope + now omitted       -> RightsDenied(CURRENTNESS_UNAVAILABLE_FAIL_CLOSED)\n9  expired credential scope + now past expiry   -> RightsDenied(EXPIRED_CREDENTIAL_SCOPE)\n10 live credential scope + now supplied         -> no raise (positive control)\n11 live entitlement + now supplied              -> allowed True (positive control)\n```\n\nHumanGate exact-bound approval — each of these must FAIL CLOSED:\n```\n12 bare string \"approved\"                      -> HumanGateBypassAttempt NOT_A_CANONICAL_APPROVAL_TOKEN\n13 bare string \"sure go ahead\"                 -> same\n14 bare string with unrelated requesting_actor -> same\n15 token with wrong subject_hash               -> DENY_EXACT_BINDING\n16 token with wrong operation                  -> DENY_EXACT_BINDING\n17 token with broader resource set             -> DENY_EXACT_BINDING\n18 token with broader scope set                -> DENY_EXACT_BINDING\n19 token with wrong environment                -> DENY_EXACT_BINDING\n20 token with wrong data_class                 -> DENY_EXACT_BINDING\n21 token expired (commit_time >= expires_at)   -> DENY_TOKEN_TIME\n22 token not yet issued (commit_time < issued_at) -> DENY_TOKEN_TIME\n23 commit_time == expires_at exactly           -> DENY_TOKEN_TIME   (equality is invalid)\n24 token_state REVOKED / CONSUMED / EXPIRED    -> DENY_TOKEN_STATE\n25 stale authn_session_generation              -> DENY_STALE_GENERATION\n26 stale credential_generation                 -> DENY_STALE_GENERATION\n27 stale rights/security/provider/ruin/consent generation -> DENY_STALE_GENERATION\n28 model/tool/provider asserted as approver    -> DENY_FALSE_AUTHORITY\n29 approver == actor (self-issued)             -> DENY_FALSE_AUTHORITY or SELF_APPROVAL_REFUSED via the seam\n30 reauthenticated_at older than max_reauth_age-> DENY_AUTHN\n31 authn_assurance_class not in AAC1..AAC3     -> DENY_AUTHN\n32 missing rollback_ref for P3                 -> DENY_NO_ROLLBACK\n33 consumer audience mismatch                  -> DENY_AUDIENCE_MISMATCH\n34 no trusted key registry                     -> DENY_TOKEN_INTEGRITY\n35 key_id not registered / wrong key_generation-> DENY_TOKEN_INTEGRITY\n36 replayed nonce (same nonce twice)           -> DENY_REPLAY\n37 T3 without independent checker evidence     -> DENY_T3_CHECKER\n38 T3 with mismatched checker evidence ref     -> DENY_T3_CHECKER\n39 bad signature shape / bad digest shape      -> DENY_TOKEN_SCHEMA\n40 wrong integrity_profile_id                  -> DENY_TOKEN_SCHEMA\n```\nPlus POSITIVE CONTROLS that must PASS:\n```\n41 fully valid independent current exact-bound token, T2/P2 -> ok True, APPROVE_BASIS_SATISFIED\n42 same token consumed once, then the seam still passes on the first use and the ledger rejects the\n   second use of the same nonce\n43 fully valid T3 token with matching independent checker evidence -> ok True\n44 nonce ledger rejects an empty or non-string nonce\n```\n\n### 5.2 `src/security/tests/test_rights.py` (modify)\n\nAny existing case that expected ENTITLED for an expiring scope with `now` omitted must be updated to the\nnew fail-closed expectation, or to supply an explicit `now`. Do not delete coverage; do not silently\nreduce the test count below the current one.\n\n## 6. Absolute rules\n\n- Fail closed everywhere. An unreadable, missing or malformed currentness/generation/key/audience input\n  denies; it never authorizes.\n- Never read the wall clock inside the library. Currentness is an explicit trusted input.\n- No new dependency, no crypto implementation, no network, no second authority system.\n- Do not weaken any other check in rights.py.\n- Keep `RightsDenied`, `HumanGateBypassAttempt`, `RightsScope`, `RightsDecision`, `HumanGateRoute`,\n  `human_gate_route`, `HIGH_RISK_ACTIONS`, `HUMAN_GATE_ROUTE`, `NONE_ROUTE` importable from\n  `src.security.rights` exactly as before; `src/security/__init__.py` must additionally export the new\n  HumanGate names.\n\n## 7. When finished print exactly one JSON object\n\n```json\n{\"files\": [\"<every path you wrote>\"], \"test_command\": \"<the command you ran>\",\n \"test_result\": \"<stdout tail>\", \"denominator\": <int number of tests collected in src/security/tests>}\n```\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
