{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_49","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\user\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -LiteralPath \\\"C:\\\\Projects\\\\Agent_Workspace\\\\HG-KSEOS\\\\var\\\\swof-construction-002-w2-repair-001\\\\specs\\\\R3_WO-SWOF-W2-R003_SPEC.md\\\" -Raw\"","aggregated_output":"# R3 WO-SWOF-W2-R003 — reach exact canonical ApprovalToken schema fidelity\n\nrepair_id: SWOF-W2-CLOSURE-R1 (corrective round R3)\norder_id: SWOF-CONSTRUCTION-002-W2-REPAIR-001\nbase: the R2 candidate (see the writer prompt for the exact SHA)\nsource: the bounded engineering-base ChangeSet authorization, section 4\n\n## 0. Why this round exists\n\nA machine diff was run against the exact canonical schema\n`swof://pi-pkg-06/doc-03/ApprovalToken/1.0.0` (PI-PKG-06::DOC-03, the JSON Schema block whose `required`\narray is quoted in the law):\n\n```\ncanonical required count : 42\nimplemented field count  : 37\nMISSING mandatory fields : if06b_version, payload_schema_version, min_reader_version,\n                           writer_version, compatibility_class, evidence_link\nconditional required     : independent_checker_evidence_ref   (already implemented)\nSCHEMA_FIDELITY          : DEVIATION\n```\n\nThe runtime type is therefore BROADER than the registry, which violates the law's rule that an\nimplementation may be STRICTER but never broader. This round closes the deviation inside the same\naffected repair cone.\n\n## 1. Files you may write (exactly these, nothing else)\n\n```\nsrc/security/humangate.py                          (modify)\nsrc/security/tests/test_humangate_currentness.py   (modify: add the cases in section 4)\nsrc/security/rights.py                             (modify ONLY if a call site needs the new fields)\nschemas/security/approval_token.schema.json        (modify: must match the canonical registry exactly)\n```\n\nPython standard library only. ASCII only. LF line endings. Do not touch any other path.\n\n## 2. Required new fields (exact names, exact semantics from the law)\n\nAdd to `ApprovalToken`, with these defaults so existing construction sites keep working, and add them to\nthe schema JSON's `required` array:\n\n| field | canonical value / type | rule |\n|---|---|---|\n| `if06b_version` | string, ABI major | default `\"1.0\"`; the ABI major must be `1` |\n| `payload_schema_version` | string | default `\"1.0.0\"` |\n| `min_reader_version` | string | default `\"1.0\"`; a reader older than this must reject |\n| `writer_version` | string | default `\"DOC03-r2\"`; an unrecognised writer is a hard failure |\n| `compatibility_class` | enum | default `\"STRICT_MAJOR_ADDITIVE_MINOR\"`; unknown class is a hard failure |\n| `evidence_link` | ref (non-empty string) | bound evidence pointer for the approval basis |\n\n`independent_checker_evidence_ref` stays as it is: it is CONDITIONALLY required when\n`independent_checker_required` is true, and must NOT be in the unconditional required list.\n\n## 3. Verification rules to add (all before the existing checks, fail closed)\n\nInsert a new ABI/envelope stage immediately after the schema-shape stage (it is part of shape, so it may\nlive in the same stage, but the reason codes below must be emitted exactly):\n\n```\n1  if06b_version missing, not a string, or its MAJOR component != \"1\"   -> \"IF06B_VERSION_UNSUPPORTED\"\n2  payload_schema_version != \"1.0.0\"                                    -> \"DENY_TOKEN_SCHEMA\"\n3  min_reader_version is newer than the reader ABI (1.0)                -> \"DENY_TOKEN_SCHEMA\"\n4  writer_version not in {\"DOC03-r2\"}                                    -> \"DENY_TOKEN_SCHEMA\"\n5  compatibility_class not in {\"STRICT_MAJOR_ADDITIVE_MINOR\"}            -> \"DENY_TOKEN_SCHEMA\"\n6  evidence_link missing, not a str, or empty after strip                -> \"DENY_TOKEN_SCHEMA\"\n```\n\nRule 2-5 are \"hard failure\" conditions in the law; keep the existing `DENY_TOKEN_SCHEMA` family so no\ndownstream consumer needs a new code, except rule 1 which has its own canonical name.\n\nKeep every other R1/R2 behaviour byte-identical in intent: exact binding, time (equality at expiry\ninvalid), state, generations, false authority, approver != actor, replay/consume-once, rollback, key\ntrust via the real verifier contract, audience, T3 checker, route re-derivation.\n\n## 4. Tests to add\n\n```\n1  a token with if06b_version \"2.0\"                     -> IF06B_VERSION_UNSUPPORTED\n2  if06b_version missing / non-string                    -> IF06B_VERSION_UNSUPPORTED\n3  payload_schema_version \"2.0.0\"                       -> DENY_TOKEN_SCHEMA\n4  writer_version \"SOMETHING-ELSE\"                      -> DENY_TOKEN_SCHEMA\n5  compatibility_class unknown                          -> DENY_TOKEN_SCHEMA\n6  evidence_link empty                                  -> DENY_TOKEN_SCHEMA\n7  min_reader_version newer than the reader             -> DENY_TOKEN_SCHEMA\n8  a fully valid token WITH all six fields set          -> APPROVE_BASIS_SATISFIED (positive control)\n9  schema-fidelity assertion: the set of names in schemas/security/approval_token.schema.json\n   \"required\" equals the canonical 42-name set (embed the canonical list in the test as a literal and\n   assert set equality, so a future drift fails loudly)\n```\n\nEvery previously passing test must still pass; the denominator may only grow.\n\n## 5. Absolute rules\n\n- The implementation must be STRICTER OR EQUAL to the canonical registry, never broader.\n- No cryptography implementation, no new dependency, no network, no wall clock.\n- Do not weaken any check added in R1 or R2.\n\n## 6. When finished print exactly one JSON object\n\n```json\n{\"files\": [\"<every path you wrote>\"], \"test_command\": \"<the command you ran>\",\n \"test_result\": \"<stdout tail>\", \"denominator\": <int tests collected in src/security/tests>,\n \"schema_required_count\": <int>}\n```\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
