{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_75","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\user\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -LiteralPath \\\"C:\\\\Projects\\\\Agent_Workspace\\\\HG-KSEOS\\\\var\\\\swof-construction-002-w2-repair-001\\\\CHANGESET_HGK_TYPED_ACCEPTANCE_RESOLUTION.md\\\" -Raw\"","aggregated_output":"# Engineering-base ChangeSet proposal — typed acceptance resolution in the HGK SharedSpine\n\nstatus: PROPOSED / NOT_ADMITTED / HITL_REQUIRED\nraised_by_order: SWOF-CONSTRUCTION-002-W2-REPAIR-001\nparent_finding: W2-POST-EXT-001 (authoritative HGK W2 normative closure never reached)\nblocks: the canonical-closure leg of SWOF-W2-CLOSURE-R1\nauthority_edge: mutation of shared HG-KSEOS core (explicit HITL)\n\n## 1. The gap, proven from source and from data\n\nRead-only evidence (`evidence/R1_HGK_CLOSURE_LEG.json`):\n\n```yaml\nproject: HGK-P0-SWOF-W2\nproject_lifecycle_state: VERIFYING\nlast_checkpoint_id: null\nworkorders: 4 -> all CREATED, result_json null\nacceptances: 4 -> all NOT_RUN, evidence_ref null\nevidence_refs: 0\ntt_records: 0\ncheckpoints: 4 -> all repo_head = 7e1f912d... (pre-mutation admission checkpoints only)\n\napi_surface:\n  acceptance_creators: [spine.py register_requirement INSERT INTO acceptances (verdict NOT_RUN)]\n  acceptance_verdict_resolvers: []          <- none anywhere in src/hg_kseos\n  acceptance_readers: [lifecycle.py denominator(): SELECT acceptance_id, verdict FROM acceptances]\n```\n\n`denominator()` counts an acceptance as an open edge while `verdict != 'PASS'`. Nothing in the typed API\ncan move `verdict` away from `NOT_RUN`, so the W2 denominator is **structurally unclosable**. The only\nway to close it would be a direct `UPDATE acceptances ...`, which the repair order forbids (\"do not\ndirect-SQL repair\"), and patching `src/hg_kseos` under this order is also forbidden.\n\nThis is a general shared-spine capability gap, not a SWOF/W2 harness defect.\n\n## 2. Proposed change (smallest correct form)\n\nAdd one typed contract to `SharedSpine`:\n\n```python\ndef resolve_acceptance(self, acceptance_id: str, *, verdict: str, evidence_ref: str,\n                       actor: str, token: str, expected_version: int,\n                       idempotency_key: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Move an acceptance from NOT_RUN to an explicit verdict, bound to an evidence ref.\n\n    Contract:\n      * verdict in {\"PASS\", \"FAIL\"} - never a free-form string\n      * evidence_ref must already exist in evidence_refs (no orphan verdicts)\n      * requires the same lease/actor/token discipline as transition_requirement\n      * emits a canonical_events row (entity_type='acceptance') with from/to state so the\n        resolution is on the append-only ordered stream, not a silent UPDATE\n      * idempotency_key makes a replay return the original event instead of re-applying\n      * expected_version guards against concurrent resolution\n    \"\"\"\n```\n\nPlus the matching `TRANSITIONS[\"acceptance\"] = {\"NOT_RUN\": {\"PASS\", \"FAIL\"}, ...}` table entry and the\n`canonical_events` entity-type registration.\n\n## 3. Why it must be a separate ChangeSet\n\n- It changes the shared contract every project depends on, not a SWOF-specific surface.\n- `record_workorder_result` already exists and is the precedent for the shape (writer != checker,\n  verdict in a closed set, evidence refs required) — but it deliberately covers WorkOrders only, and\n  extending its meaning silently would be a semantic drift.\n- The repair order explicitly routes this case to a separate engineering-base ChangeSet.\n\n## 4. Acceptance test sketch for the ChangeSet\n\n```\n1  resolve_acceptance on an existing NOT_RUN acceptance with a registered evidence ref -> verdict set,\n   canonical event emitted, version incremented\n2  resolve_acceptance with an unregistered evidence_ref -> InvariantViolation ERR_EVIDENCE_UNKNOWN\n3  resolve_acceptance with verdict \"MAYBE\" -> InvariantViolation ERR_ACCEPTANCE_VERDICT\n4  replay with the same idempotency_key -> idempotent_replay True, no second event\n5  stale expected_version -> StaleState\n6  after resolution, denominator(project) reports acceptances_open == 0 for that project\n7  a project with one open acceptance reports required_local_scope_open >= 1 and\n   completion_sweep classifies it as auto_local\n```\n\n## 5. Effect on the SWOF W2 repair\n\nOnce admitted, the SWOF repair resumes at exactly one step: project the already-frozen,\nalready-verified, subject-bound evidence into the W2 spine through typed calls\n(`register_evidence`, `record_workorder_result`, `resolve_acceptance`, `open_tt`, `checkpoint`), then\nre-issue the LocalClosureReceipt and republish. No product byte needs to change to do that.\n\nUntil then the canonical-closure leg is `TEMP_CLOSED_STATE` for the exact reason in §1, and W3 remains\non HOLD.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
